     German seller invoicing a VAT-registered business in another EU member state (France)
     for goods shipped across the border — an innergemeinschaftliche Lieferung (§ 4 Nr. 1b /
     § 6a UStG, EU VAT Directive art. 138). The supply is exempt under VAT category K, so
     EVERY line carries CategoryCode K at RateApplicablePercent 0 and the invoice shows ZERO
     VAT. Exercises the K family no other CII fixture touches:
       * BT-31 seller VAT id (DE000000000, VAT-scoped ram:SpecifiedTaxRegistration schemeID
         'VA') AND BT-48 buyer VAT id (FR00000000000, also VAT-scoped) — BR-IC-02 needs BOTH;
       * two K lines at rate 0 (BR-IC-05);
       * exactly one K VAT breakdown (BR-IC-01) with BT-116 = Σ K nets = 10500.00 and
         BT-117 = 0.00 (BR-IC-08/09);
       * the mandated intra-community exemption reason on that breakdown: BT-121 code
         VATEX-EU-IC (on the CEF VATEX list, BR-CL-22) AND BT-120 text (BR-IC-10);
       * the two K-only document requirements the AE reverse-charge family has no analogue
         for: BR-IC-11 (BT-72 actual delivery date via ram:ActualDeliverySupplyChainEvent/
         ram:OccurrenceDateTime/udt:DateTimeString) AND BR-IC-12 (BT-80 deliver-to country
         via ram:ShipToTradeParty/ram:PostalTradeAddress/ram:CountryID = FR).
     Arithmetic reconciles across the breakdown/totals; no other rule fires. -->
